 "assumptions": [
  "The period follows the small-swing formula: period = 2π × √(length ÷ gravity).",
  "The string has no mass and does not stretch, and all the bob's mass sits at one point. There is no air resistance or friction.",
  "The motion is worked out from the scene clock, so changing the length or gravity restarts the swing at the new rate from the current time. The bob may jump to a new spot when you do this."
